※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4905

※ A clause is over values or over types and not both.  The reading that makes
※ the type operand legal is the reading that stops checking the half that is
※ about values, and a condition silently becoming a requirement is the one
※ failure mode this notation could have -- so it is refused, and two clauses
※ say it.

fn total(a: T', n: u64) → T' pre(n > 0u64 ∧ T' ⊞ T' → T'):
    a

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    ⎕narrow(total(3u8, 1u64), ⌜u6⌝) ?? 1u6
